Brief Description:

This is a blockchain-based evidence chain of custody system which can record all evidence
actions as immutable blocks in a binary file. Actions such as add, checkout, checkin, remove - 
creates a new block linked via SHA-256 hashes which makes tampering detectable.


How everything works:

Five main components:

1. block.py - This file contains block structure with binary packing 
2. blockchain.py - This has multiple components like file management, validation and hash chain verification
3. crypto_utils.py - AES-ECB encryption for case IDs
4. commands.py - This is the command implementations
5. bchoc.py - CLI interface 

The case IDs (UUID) and item IDs (integers) are encrypted before storing.
Each block stores: previous hash, timestamp, encrypted IDs, state, creator, 
owner, & optional data.


Installation:

pip install pycryptodome --break-system-packages
make


Commands:

./bchoc init
./bchoc add -c <case_id> -i <item_id> -g <creator> -p C67C
./bchoc checkout -i <item_id> -p <password>
./bchoc checkin -i <item_id> -p <password>
./bchoc remove -i <item_id> -y <DISPOSED|DESTROYED|RELEASED> -p C67C
./bchoc show cases
./bchoc show items -c <case_id>
./bchoc show history [-c <case_id>] [-i <item_id>] [-n <num>] [-r] -p <password>
./bchoc verify
./bchoc summary -c <case_id>


Passwords:

C67C - CREATOR (required for add/remove)
P80P - POLICE
L76L - LAWYER
A65A - ANALYST
E69E - EXECUTIVE


State Rules:

- New items: CHECKEDIN
- Checkout only if CHECKEDIN
- Checkin only if CHECKEDOUT
- Remove only if CHECKEDIN
- No actions after DISPOSED/DESTROYED/RELEASED


Examples:

./bchoc init
./bchoc add -c 65cc391d-6568-4dcc-a978-c0a8c5f1f4f9 -i 12345 -g JohnDoe -p C67C
./bchoc checkout -i 12345 -p A65A
./bchoc checkin -i 12345 -p L76L
./bchoc show history -i 12345 -p E69E
./bchoc verify
./bchoc summary -c 65cc391d-6568-4dcc-a978-c0a8c5f1f4f9
./bchoc remove -i 12345 -y DISPOSED -p C67C


Technical details:

- File: blockchain.dat
- Encryption: AES-ECB, 16-byte output as 32-char hex string
- Hashing: SHA-256
- Format: Binary (big-endian integers)